# boot-timing overlay notes. NO BASE_SHA256 here, deliberately: this patch NEVER
# replaces an upstream file. It injects sitecustomize.py via PYTHONPATH and wraps
# upstream functions post-import, looked up by name at import time. If upstream
# renames/removes a target the hook no-ops and the report prints "hooks NOT
# applied: <list>" -- the boot itself is untouched either way. So nothing to
# re-derive on snapshot bumps; only a shrinking report would ever signal drift.
# (Since 2026-10-15 this is also the general rule rather than a contrast: the one
# overlay that DID copy an upstream file, qwen3.8-flash-next/patches/ple-ct-ignore,
# was removed once vllm#59431 landed upstream, so no patch here carries a hash.)
