# Memory + headroom report (2026-09-25): the gpu_worker/model_runner rows
# above gained mem= OPTIONS on the SAME wrapper, emitting mem.* marks
# (device/cfg/load/prof/kvbudget/kv/kvcfg/gr+phase/final/host0) that sample
# torch.cuda and /proc around the already-hooked calls. THE HOOK TABLE IS
# UNCHANGED — no new module, no new attribute, so ZERO new drift surface: a
# drifted target loses its timing row and its memory row together, through
# the same "hooks NOT applied" note. The KV cache is the only
# gpu_memory_utilization-scaled component, so the report's hard/safe util
# floors are exact arithmetic on measured bytes (hard=non_kv/total,
# safe=ceil2dp((non_kv+1GiB+max(1.5GiB,2%total))/total)). Without
# torch/CUDA the samplers record nothing and the memory sections vanish
# ("memory: insufficient marks") — never a boot-path failure. BOOT_TIMING=0
# still disables EVERYTHING, memory sampling included. The WEIGHT LOAD line
# carries an effective GPU-placement rate " @ 170 MiB/s (47.3 GiB)" from the
# same mem.load marks (worker.load is the only whitelisted span: a KV "rate"
# would measure cudaMalloc caching, a host-pin one cudaHostRegister fill).
